"help.body" = "1  Scan: hold one face of the cube to the camera. When the grid locks on and the outline fills up, the face is captured. Show the other faces one by one, in any order; all six are needed.\n\n2  Check: once recognised, the whole cube is shown as a map. If the colours match, tap “Start solving”.\n\n3  Solve: any face can point at the camera; there's no need to look for a particular colour. Instructions follow the way you hold the cube, such as “Turn the top layer left” or “Turn the right layer up”, and the small cube in the top corner is held the same way as yours. When the camera sees a move completed, the next one appears by itself; for the few moves the camera can't see, you'll be told what to do, and you can always tap “Next”.\n\nNotation: as you hold the cube, R L U D F B are the right, left, top, bottom, front and back layers, M is the middle column and E the middle row. A plain letter means clockwise (looking at that layer), ′ means counterclockwise and 2 means a half turn.\n\nTips: keep your fingers off the stickers; in dim light, tap the torch at the top right.";
